+/**
+ * Editing a Flow List's Spline path on the UMG designer's canvas, as a Custom Shape's outline is edited (see
+ * WidgetShapePathEditor.h) - instead of typing Spline Points into the Details panel.
+ *
+ * For a selected Flow List whose Layout > Type is Spline, a designer extension puts a toolbar above it (Edit Path; while
+ * editing, Done, the Select and Pen tools, Reverse, Delete) and - while editing - a layer over it that draws the curve
+ * items are laid along, its points, and the focus marker, and takes the mouse and keyboard. See the class comment of
+ * SFlowListPathCanvas in the .cpp for every gesture.
+ *
+ * Edits go to the Widget Blueprint's own Flow List (the template, which is saved) and to the designer's preview of it, so
+ * the items move along the new curve at once; each drag or key is one undo step. Whether it is editing, which tool and
+ * which points are selected are kept here by the list's name, so the designer rebuilding its canvas widgets mid-edit goes
+ * unnoticed.
+ */
